<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Central Puerto buys back $17.5 mln debt.</title>
<headline>Argentine Central Puerto buys back $17.5 mln debt.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's electricity generating company Central Puerto SA said Thursday it has bought back $17.5 million of its $100 million bond issue.</p>
<p>The company said it had received notice from Citibank NA, the depository bank for the bonds, that the amount was cancelled.</p>
<p>The bond carries a coupon of 10.75 percent and matures on November 2, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 3180668</p>
</text>
